# ==========================================================
# ENV FILES
#
# This block was missing, which is how frontend/.env ended up committed. Vite
# inlines every VITE_* value into the public JS bundle at build time, so a
# frontend env file can never hold a real secret - but it does hold per-env
# config, and a committed one silently fights the value the host sets. Track
# .env.example, ignore the rest.
# ==========================================================
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
